_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in Chrome for Android 136 on multiple devices\nGodot 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot 4.4 - Chrome for Android 136\n\n### Issue description\n\nI created a minimal WebXR project with the reference code from https://docs.godotengine.org/de/4.x/classes/class_webxrinterface.html\n\nThe project runs correctly on Meta Quest 2. On Android Smartphones with Chrome, it writes on the console:\n\n> OpenGL API OpenGL ES 3.0 (WebGL 2.0 (OpenGL ES 3.0 Chromium)) - Compatibility - Using Device: WebKit - WebKit WebGL\n\nBut then _webxr_session_failed() throws:\n\n> Unable to make webgl context compatible with webxr. Typerror: godotwebxr.gl_binding.createProjectionLayer is not a function\n\nBoth the error message (Unable to make...) and the call of createProjectionLayer are part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/978b38797ba8e8757592f21101e32e364d60662d/modules/webxr/native/library_godot_webxr.js#L103\n\nMaybe this is a timing issue when createProjectionLayer is not yet available?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create minimal XR Scene with Node3D, XROrigin3D, XRCamera3D and a Button\n- Add the example script from https://docs.godotengine.org/de/4.x/classes/class_webxrinterface.html\n- In Preferences, check the OpenXR checkboxes **enabled** and Shaders \"\"enabled\"\".\n- Export to Web\n- Copy to HTTPS Webspace\n- Run on Phone\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot project dependend, issue occurs in very basic WebXR projects","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"ht